{"id": "EUVD-2026-101070", "enisaUuid": "da86a1fd-b70f-3591-a249-a0664ff61c71", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: require a peer station for TDLS setup confirm\n\nIt's nonsense for the setup confirm to go to station that\ndoesn't even exist, and it hits a warning when building\nthe frame:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(!sta || !ap_sta)\n\nOnly accept WLAN_TDLS_SETUP_CONFIRM when the station is\nalready there as a TDLS station. Need to copy the call\nto ieee80211_tdls_prep_mgmt_packet() since the existing\nWLAN_TDLS_DISCOVERY_REQUEST already falls through to it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bae6ef511a29ef12ab969adeea691067d4d5d74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0afa5395c46d73ad2090aa50209886e84f179bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/742c762bee59c973684f70dfed7de4945d3141e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fce36d242a18ddf64731d816a37564103172da11", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c0a5c96473b9e7a5f4c453ef6a13dc0f5589a4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/038e1d126304fd25d507fd4e671232df57bd1799"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98421", "GHSA-6hcf-6997-pq7q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "26693807-6e31-39d9-8005-ab164504e8ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f7eaa47e1de30159277f91f1145a6687f13ffd9 <038e1d126304fd25d507fd4e671232df57bd1799"}, {"id": "2b801fef-c23e-3cdb-8ad5-8faad32ccc2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "3785df8b-cf5f-379d-b1d7-c274d3fb2c24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "483e51a1-bb84-38f2-91fc-9de58ce479d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f7eaa47e1de30159277f91f1145a6687f13ffd9 <fce36d242a18ddf64731d816a37564